  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Expand and simplify (x + 9)(x − 1)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: The −1 still produces a full x-term, so do not let its size fool you."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p053_q05.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p053-q05 from workbook page 53."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Multiply the first terms.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "x × x"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: x²"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Multiply the outer and inner pairs.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "x × (−1) = −x and 9 × x = 9x"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: −x + 9x"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Multiply the last terms.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "9 × (−1)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: −9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Collect the middle terms.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "9x − x = 8x"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: x² + 8x − 9"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Multiply out all four products, then combine the like terms."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "x² + 8x − 9"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "The distributive law generates four products, and the two containing a single x combine into the middle term. Here 9 + (−1) = 8 and 9 × (−1) = −9, so the quadratic is x² + 8x − 9. The negative constant confirms that the two brackets have opposite signs, exactly as they do."
    }
  ],
